                <pb facs="0403" n="295" sameAs="frus:frus1927v02/pg295"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">393.1163/171: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Consul General at
                        Shanghai</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Gauss</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1927-04-29T18:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">April 29,
                                1927—6 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>Your April 16, 4 p.m. Department informed Mission has telegraphed missionaries to
                    conform with your recommendations.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kellogg</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
